// Preferred way
if (str.isEmpty()) {
    // String is empty
}

// Less preferred, but equivalent
if (str.length() == 0) {
    // String is empty
}

If beginIndex equals endIndex, the result is an empty string. This is a valid operation and doesn't throw an exception. For example:

String str = "Hello";
String empty = str.substring(2, 2); // empty is ""
